  "details": "As we all know, turning cloning on and off in VRC is one of the most essential features. Very commonly do strangers, friends and more approach others and request to clone, copy, take, whatever the word may be. There's nothing more awkward than the 10 second wait time for someone to open their settings menu to check that very tiny box, and then back out of their menus. They then have to quickly enter the menu again and as quickly as they can turn cloning off to avoid randoms from sniping their avatar. \nTo greatly improve the user experience, the hand menu should include a switch button that turns cloning on and off instantly. Even better, why not also have the ability to toggle individual players' abilities to override your clone settings, similarly to how one toggles players to ignore their safety settings. These features not only make avatar cloning less stressful, but also easier, more accessible to newer users, and more common. There could even be some additional settings in the full settings menu to all friends only to clone your avatars. \nThe basic and stressful system of sharing avatars, which is especially tense in public worlds from fear of random avatar thieves, is outdated. This update doesn't have any negatives from a user viewpoint aside from the hand-menu icons possibly needing to shrink slightly to make room, another tab being added, so forth. Such expansions seem easy and without much inconvenience to the existing UI.",
